# sanitize-pdf scope-switch audit — every switch driven ON and OFF, the produced bytes diffed
# Build: `sweep/optimize` rebased onto master (`1376101`), dev server http://localhost:5295,
#   Chromium over CDP 9845, `docs/research/colour-rail.mjs` with `docs/research/sanitize-switch-spec.json` (60 runs).
# Fixtures: `python3 docs/research/sanitize-switch-fixtures.py --dir /tmp/lane-optimize2/fx` (6 files) plus the committed
#   foreign banks `tests/fixtures/{foreign,attachments}/` and `/tmp/triage/in/{annot,meta}.pdf`.
# Judged by: `python3 docs/research/sanitize-switch-measure.py --spec … --runs … --outdir …` (this file); every needle is
#   derived from the untouched fixture, and "removed" is a search of every object source and decoded stream MuPDF can name,
#   in both PDF escape spellings, plus the raw file bytes.
# Reading (the six switches, current build):
#   * Remove JavaScript and automatic actions — MOVES BYTES on every shape driven: 5/5 payloads
#     gone on the six-scope file (an `/OpenAction` array with one referenced and one inline action,
#     a page `/AA`, a JS link, a `/Kids` script tree with an inline leaf), poppler flips
#     `JavaScript: yes → no`, 4/4 on `script-hosts-aa`, 2/2 on `script-names-kids`.
#   * Remove embedded files — MOVES BYTES: 2/2 payloads gone on the six-scope file and on
#     `attach-foreign`, 1/1 on `mupdf-native`, 2/2 through a `/Kids` tree, and on every other shape
#     driven (9 files). Reader answers change (`pdfdetach` lists nothing, no `/EmbeddedFile` left).
#   * Remove hidden layer content — MOVES BYTES: the `/OFF` layer's operators leave the page's own
#     content stream (2 payload copies on two files) with the visible layer untouched and the
#     drawing unmoved (0 px outside any mark).
#   * Remove the document info dictionary — MOVES BYTES when the trailer names it by reference
#     (2/2 and 4/4 payloads gone, poppler's `Title:` line goes blank); **the ON and OFF outputs are
#     byte-identical on `info-inline.pdf`, whose trailer holds `/Info << … >>` directly**, and the
#     card then says "there was no info dictionary" over a file poppler still titles.
#   * Remove XMP metadata — **takes the pointer and ships the payload.** The catalogue's `/Metadata`
#     is gone (poppler: `Metadata Stream: no`), the packet's own stream is still in the file at its
#     old object number, referenced by nothing: 2/2 needles on `all.pdf` (2260 → 2250 B), 1/1 on the
#     MuPDF-written `metadata.pdf` (2765 → 2756 B) and on `/tmp/triage/in/meta.pdf` (3303 → 3296 B).
#     The card says "XMP metadata removed".
#   * Remove annotations and form fields — **same defect, bigger cargo.** `/Annots` empties, the
#     marks come off the page (1825 px on the six-scope file, 573 px on `annot.pdf`, 11 854 px on the
#     foreign `annotations.pdf`), MuPDF lists no annotation — and every annotation dictionary, its
#     appearance stream and the whole field subtree stay in the download: 5/5 payloads on `all.pdf`,
#     9/9 on `annotations.pdf` ("A note from an outside writer" is in the output either way), the
#     filled-in answer on `form.pdf`. The card says "5 annotation(s) removed".
#   * Control that no switch is a re-renderer: 0 px moved outside an annotation rectangle in all 60
#     runs (poppler renders, 110 dpi, >16/255), page counts unchanged, content streams byte-identical
#     unless the layer switch was on. `annot-inherited.pdf` (/Annots on the `/Pages` node) is the one
#     shape where ON and OFF are identical *and* no reader reaches the payload in the source —
#     recorded, not counted as a defect.
#   * Network half: 60/60 runs report "1 request(s), 0 off-origin" — no file byte left the tab; the
#     single request is the tool page itself. No console errors in any run.
#

# sanitize-pdf switch audit — 60 run(s)


